{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"929377169382ef94fc9269f7b427e160a7f1389beabc8063e166afe4fd74a0d3","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot container, Bedrock LLM integration","key_entities":["REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py::build_bedrock_provider","BedrockProvider","boto3.session.Session().region_name","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py","LLMConfigError"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock","region","aws","configuration","cutover","noregionerror","review-bot"],"propositions":["The review-bot container environment does not set AWS_DEFAULT_REGION or REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, causing boto3.session.Session().region_name to resolve to None","build_bedrock_provider passes region=None to BedrockProvider when REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION is unset, triggering a NoRegionError from boto3 at client construction with no catchable LLMError handler","IMDS reachability does not supply a region to boto3; region configuration is independent of IMDS/hop-limit contingency","boto3 recognizes AWS_DEFAULT_REGION for region resolution but not AWS_REGION in standard botocore session initialization","The cutover lacks cross-provider fallback, so a missing Bedrock region takes down the LLM-Review gate entirely rather than degrading to another model"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787321641421322001,"uuid":"10e6b632-9c2b-4c88-9175-77f91db1f92b"}